 "note": "Fryberger & Dean (1979) drift potential, DP = sum V^2 (V - 12 kt)/100 * t with V the hourly-mean 10 m wind in knots and t each hour's share of its year in percent; DP, RDP are mean annual values in vector units (VU/yr). RDD_deg is the direction sand moves TO (resultant of downwind drift vectors), degrees clockwise from north. sand_rose.sector_deg is the direction the wind blows FROM (16 sectors of 22.5 deg centred on sector_deg); sand_rose.dp sums to DP. Data: MERRA-2 tavg1_2d_slv_Nx via Earth Engine NASA/GSFC/MERRA/slv/2, native cell centred 24.0 N 55.625 E (spans 23.75-24.25 N, 55.3125-55.9375 E; 0.5 x 0.625 deg, about 55 x 63 km) containing the box centroid (100.0 % of the box lies in it); Earth Engine's grid is offset from the native one, so the pixel was chosen by native index and checked against NASA POWER. Missing hours: 0 of 219168. NASA POWER cross-check 2001-2024: DP differs by 0.001 %, RDD by 0.004 deg (same underlying MERRA-2, so this checks processing only). Caveat: a ~50 km reanalysis of hourly means damps gusts, so absolute DP is likely biased low against station anemometers and dp_class is approximate; RDD and RDP_DP are the more robust outputs. Computed by pipeline/01_scenes_and_wind.ipynb."
